From 445e22775a5e9da6b1bb88cde81db86f08a812bc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: BillYuan01 <40728295+BillYuan01@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 14:31:17 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(harnesses): add USAGE event channel for backend token
 usage

Third-party backends could not report token or context usage even
though HarnessCapabilities.context_usage advertised the capability:
there was neither an event kind nor a landing path.

Add HarnessEventKind.USAGE plus a typed HarnessUsage payload carried in
a new optional HarnessEvent.usage field. The field keeps every existing
adapter working unchanged (defaults to None). The runtime consumes USAGE
as side-channel metadata without emitting text/tool envelopes or failing
the turn, and stages it through a new
TokenRecordingModelWrapper.record_usage_for_session entry point so the
existing channel turn-usage commit path (SSE + persistence) picks it up.
---
